  ],
  "text": "A lightning bolt is five times hotter than the surface of the Sun. You make lightning yourself. Every time you touch a door handle in winter. Same physics, both times. Rub two things together and the charge separates. Inside a storm cloud, ice does the rubbing. Millions of collisions every second. Light ice floats up positive. Heavy hail sinks down negative. The gap grows. When that gap finally breaks, thirty thousand amps take the shortest way down. Thunder is not the strike. It is air heated so fast that it explodes. So when you count the seconds, you are just listening to the air catch up. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
